      "why": "HELD OUT by user ruling 2026-08-01 (Issue #261 wave-2 packet, item 2b). The ruling is REJECT -- the agent should attack with Jetting Blow, as the correction states -- and the cause is a FITTED CONSTANT sitting inside its own margin, which a refresh swap must not re-fit.\n\nMEASURED. All three held cards cover exactly one general slot each, so the shed IS the haircut sum:\n  Ignition Energy 30 x 0.45 = 13.5 | Basic {W} 8 x 0.45 = 3.6 | Wally's 20 x 0.45 = 9.0\n  total 26.1 -- the shed, exactly. v1 charged 29.4 (same cards, full tier, re-access only).\nThe whole -1.4 -> +1.9 flip is _GENERAL_WORTH_W = 0.45. The swing declines iff shed > 28.0, i.e. 58 x W > 28, i.e. W > 0.483. The constant is 0.45 -- this frame sits 7% away from a fitted number.\n\nNOT re-fitted here, deliberately. _GENERAL_WORTH_W was measured (WP-N5: under-pricing 46->19 came from W alone) and pilot._refresh_slot_resupply's docstring carries a standing instruction: 'Re-open only as a JOINT re-measure of W and r, never r alone.' Moving W to satisfy one frame is the rung-fitting the POC exists to delete, and it would move every keep-value site including the discard decider's 12/12.\n\nTWO THEORIES TESTED AND REFUTED, so the owner need not re-run them:\n  * the deferred 'non-Active fund bodies' leg -- the bench holds a 2nd Mega Starmie ex on 1     {W} needing 3, so fund slots were prototyped for benched bodies: shed 26.10 -> 26.10, no     movement. The Energy already sit on general slots worth more than ENERGY_TIER 8, so the     assignment does not re-route them.\n  * the insurance slot (ADR-0101, which fixes ep83969481 f55) -- correctly declines here: a     SECOND Mega Starmie ex sits undamaged on the bench, so the line survives the Active's KO     and nothing irreplaceable is being insured.\n\nReturns to gating when W and r are jointly re-measured -- delete this owner then.\n\nOWNER: #272 (POC-B2, term-weight calibration) -- it owns exactly this question, whether the agent's fitted term weights sit right, and _GENERAL_WORTH_W is one of them."
